figures-without-finetuning/
# Slurm opens --output/--error before the job script runs, so slurm_logs/ must
# already exist at submit time - a `mkdir -p` inside the script is too late.
# Keep the directory itself tracked, ignore the logs written into it.
slurm_logs/*
!slurm_logs/.gitkeep
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.safetensors

# ------------------------------------------- Uncompressed dataset splits (BIG)
# The dataset ships gzipped. Plain train.jsonl is 205 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit, and committing it once already made this repo unpushable.
# Anchored to the dataset folder so reports/*.jsonl still commits.
/united-cryptonite-wordplay-dataset/train.jsonl
/united-cryptonite-wordplay-dataset/val.jsonl
/united-cryptonite-wordplay-dataset/test.jsonl

# --------------------------------------------------- Third-party source datasets
# Not committed: re-downloadable, and cryptonite-train.jsonl is 102 MB.
#   Cryptonite : https://github.com/aviaefrat/cryptonite
#   Wordplay   : https://github.com/mdda/cryptic-wordplay
cryptonite-official-split/
cryptic-wordplay-main/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Local tool state
.claude/settings.local.json

# ==============================================================================
# Deliberately COMMITTED, do not add ignore rules for these:
#   united-cryptonite-wordplay-dataset/*.jsonl.gz    (18.6 / 1.1 / 1.1 MB)
#   united-cryptonite-wordplay-dataset/reports/*.jsonl   (audit trail, 0.4 MB)
#   stats.json  build_united_dataset.py  verify_dataset.py  README.md  code/
# The rules above are anchored or path-scoped on purpose - a bare `*.jsonl` or
# `*.gz` rule would silently swallow the dataset itself.
# ==============================================================================
